course: dictionary
lesson: 5523
title: Leather: a material and a describing word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Leather is a strong material made from animal skin that has been treated so it does not rot. Use the context to check: «Kid gloves are gloves of soft leather from young goats.» Here leather is the stuff the gloves are made from.
explain: Leather can also describe things. In «a leather jacket» or «leather shoes», the word leather tells you what the jacket or shoes are made of. Test it by swapping in «made of leather»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Sailors ate sawdust and leather, and many died of scurvy» shows that they had almost no food, because the sentence tells you scurvy comes from a lack of fresh fruit and vegetables. Leather was not a treat there. Some leather is not from animals at all: vegan leather is made from plastics or plants.
fact: Leather is a tough, flexible material, and it is fairly waterproof.
fact: «Leather» can be a noun for the material, or an adjective describing something, as in «leather shoes».
fact: Leather was used in history for armour, saddles and buckets.
fact: In «kid gloves», «kid» means a young goat, not a child.
fact: Synthetic or vegan leather is made from plastics or plants, not from animal skin.
exercise: «Kid gloves are gloves of soft leather from young goats.» What is leather? | *A material made from animal skin, treated so it does not rot | A type of wood used for boats | A kind of cloth woven from plants | A metal used for making swords
exercise: In «a leather jacket», what does leather do? | It names the person who made the jacket | It tells you the jacket is wet | *It tells you what the jacket is made of | It means the jacket is very old
exercise: «He is cut off when he sees a chauffeur in leather gaiters and two large rural policemen running after him.» Find and copy one word that means a paid car driver. | policemen | gaiters | *chauffeur | fields
test: Which of these is real leather? | A wooden spoon | A plastic football | *A football made from treated animal skin | A paper bag
test: «Sailors ate sawdust and leather, and many died of scurvy.» What does this sentence show? | *Food was so scarce that they ate things that were not food | Leather is full of fresh fruit and vegetables | Sailors were rich and had plenty to eat | Sailors liked the taste of leather very much
exam: Sam says «leather» can only ever be a noun. Is he right? | Yes, it is always a noun and never anything else | *No, it can also be an adjective, as in «leather shoes» | No, it is always a number | Yes, it is always a verb, meaning to hit
